But why would Aoshima be getting
in our Senior's way?

14:42.810 --> 14:45.550
Because, unlike me, Yamano
is loved by everyone.

14:45.550 --> 14:46.510
Huh?

14:47.010 --> 14:48.640
Let's go to the university.

14:49.580 --> 14:51.380
Is the date over already?

14:51.820 --> 14:56.050
Please tell Otaki that it might be
a good idea to go to campus.

14:56.360 --> 14:57.650
Oh, okay...

14:58.930 --> 15:00.150
Dai-chan...

15:01.630 --> 15:04.150
Live it up for me, too, man...

15:06.500 --> 15:08.970
You think it looks all right?

15:08.970 --> 15:10.770
It's very cute.

15:11.040 --> 15:14.840
I'm sorry to have you come along to help me
with a project I had forgotten about.

15:15.010 --> 15:18.410
Ah, it's nothing! I'm glad to be
helping you out!

15:18.410 --> 15:20.610
B-But you don't have to single out
only one of them.

15:20.610 --> 15:23.050
I brought a few of them...

15:23.050 --> 15:24.820
That's awesome.

15:24.820 --> 15:27.090
It really gets my creative juices flowing.

15:27.090 --> 15:29.560
I'm so glad you're giving me
a hand with this!

15:29.820 --> 15:31.660
Y-You mean it?!

15:31.660 --> 15:32.560
Yes!

15:34.560 --> 15:39.170
Hey, Satoko, do you think I'm
a weirdo or anything?

15:39.170 --> 15:41.140
No, I don't at all.

15:41.140 --> 15:45.010
Thanks to your interest, I've got you
here helping me with this project.

15:45.010 --> 15:46.630
Satoko!

15:47.310 --> 15:49.140
The model's not supposed to move!

15:49.140 --> 15:50.170
Uh, right!

15:51.010 --> 15:53.110
They seem to be enjoying themselves.

15:53.110 --> 15:55.670
I guess we're no longer needed here.

15:56.020 --> 15:57.950
Damn it!

15:58.350 --> 16:01.220
There's no way I'm going to let things
keep going so smoothly!

16:04.760 --> 16:08.200
I'm sorry you always have to
come along to my lectures.

16:08.200 --> 16:11.670
Why do you apologize? I enjoy it.

16:11.670 --> 16:14.230
Huh... Is that right?

16:14.230 --> 16:15.500
Yes!

16:15.500 --> 16:18.140
You seem to be having fun, too.

16:18.140 --> 16:19.840
You think so?

16:19.840 --> 16:21.140
Yes, I do.

16:21.640 --> 16:23.300
Belldandy...

16:23.910 --> 16:25.240
Keiichi...

16:25.680 --> 16:27.150
Morisato!

16:27.310 --> 16:29.750
She... She invited me to her PLACE!

16:29.750 --> 16:31.340
That's great!

16:31.650 --> 16:34.560
Hey, I'm not used to this kind of stuff, man!

16:34.560 --> 16:36.420
Well, I'm certainly not either!

16:36.420 --> 16:40.030
But you're the one who's been goin'
steady with Bell for a whole year!

16:40.030 --> 16:42.860
For starters, I think it would be a good idea

16:42.860 --> 16:45.370
to come across as clean-cut
as you possibly can,

16:45.370 --> 16:49.570
and to act like a chivalrous knight,
a perfect gentleman.

16:49.570 --> 16:51.570
Clean-cut and chivalrous, huh?

16:51.570 --> 16:52.540
All right!

16:53.240 --> 16:54.540
How about that?

16:55.210 --> 16:57.880
Satoko said this one was cool, too!

16:57.880 --> 16:59.870
She said LIKE a chivalrous knight...

17:00.780 --> 17:02.650
Then how about this?!

17:02.650 --> 17:05.880
What if you were to go for something
a little more NORMAL?

17:06.150 --> 17:09.590
I'm thinking Satoko would enjoy
something like this more.

17:09.590 --> 17:10.720
Ah...

17:13.030 --> 17:15.530
Does this really work?

17:15.530 --> 17:17.600
Doesn't the suit of armor look better?

17:17.600 --> 17:20.070
Oh, come on! I'm telling you it's fine!

17:20.330 --> 17:22.970
When you get there,
give this bouquet to her,

17:22.970 --> 17:28.170
and say, "Thank you so very much
for the invitation."

17:28.580 --> 17:30.040
Thanks, Bell!

17:30.310 --> 17:32.970
All right, I'm off!

17:33.880 --> 17:35.980
I told you the armor is no good!

17:35.980 --> 17:38.710
Huh? But Satoko says it's cool!

17:38.950 --> 17:42.960
Crap! At this rate, he's going to
steal Satoko from me!

17:42.960 --> 17:44.790
What the heck am I going to do?

17:44.790 --> 17:46.420
What are you doing?

17:47.030 --> 17:49.400
What are you doing back here?

17:49.400 --> 17:51.930
That's it! Sayoko! I have a favor to ask you!

17:51.930 --> 17:52.960
Favor?

17:58.170 --> 18:01.070
Th-That's a big-ass house...

18:04.880 --> 18:06.210
Yamano Residence.

18:06.210 --> 18:10.240
Th-Thank you so very much for
the invitation here today.

18:12.050 --> 18:15.420
Um, this is just a trifle
I have to offer you...

18:15.420 --> 18:17.650
My, my, how thoughtful.

18:18.030 --> 18:20.560
S-Satoko, did you catch
a cold or something...

18:20.560 --> 18:21.530
Huh?!

18:22.000 --> 18:24.290
Ugh, I wonder if this is gonna work...

18:29.870 --> 18:32.270
Aoshima? AND Sayoko?!

18:32.610 --> 18:34.410
What are you doing here?

18:34.410 --> 18:36.510
Ah, I've been waiting for you, Sayoko.

18:36.510 --> 18:38.840
Is he the one you wanted to introduce to me?

18:39.110 --> 18:41.010
Yes, he is, president Yamano.

18:41.010 --> 18:42.420
President?

18:42.420 --> 18:44.710
This is Aoshima, the president of
the Four Wheels Club.

18:45.090 --> 18:46.950
How have you been, sir?
Didn't you know that Satoko's father
is the president of Nekomi Tech?

18:46.950 --> 18:50.460
Ah, well if it isn't the Aoshimas' son!
Didn't you know that Satoko's father
is the president of Nekomi Tech?

18:50.460 --> 18:50.890
Didn't you know that Satoko's father
is the president of Nekomi Tech?

18:50.890 --> 18:52.190
Otaki!

18:53.160 --> 18:54.700
Satoko!

18:54.700 --> 18:56.860
Is this man here to see you?

18:56.860 --> 18:59.870
Yes. Dad, this is Otaki, from the Auto Club.

18:59.870 --> 19:01.470
Auto Club?

19:01.470 --> 19:03.470
It-It's nice to meet you.

19:03.470 --> 19:06.540
That's right. The infamous Auto Club.

19:06.540 --> 19:07.940
What did you say?!
Their ill reputation was my reason for
creating the Four Wheels Club.

19:07.940 --> 19:09.240
Their ill reputation was my reason for
creating the Four Wheels Club.

19:09.540 --> 19:12.810
Actually, we're here today to ask you
about that. What do you think?

19:12.810 --> 19:17.440
Now that we have the Four Wheels Club,
why not disband the Auto Club?

19:17.850 --> 19:19.990
W-What the hell are you talking about?!

19:19.990 --> 19:23.090
Oh, my. Perhaps we should talk about
its reputation on campus?

19:23.090 --> 19:26.250
But if we do, then simply disbanding
the club may not be enough...

19:27.260 --> 19:28.690
Otaki...

19:29.160 --> 19:32.070
Things have gotten pretty grim over there.

19:32.070 --> 19:33.870
It will be all right.

19:33.870 --> 19:37.130
There is still good fortune around Otaki.

19:37.870 --> 19:39.300
I'll be back in a minute, okay?

19:41.010 --> 19:43.030
It smells like something's burning.

19:43.480 --> 19:45.880
Oh, no! I left the food on the stove!

19:45.880 --> 19:46.680
Huh?!

19:48.380 --> 19:49.450
Oh, no!

19:49.450 --> 19:50.650
Holy crap!

19:50.650 --> 19:51.190
Someone get some water!

19:51.190 --> 19:52.120
No, not water!
Someone get some water!

19:52.120 --> 19:52.850
Can you do something, Aoshima?
No, not water!

19:52.850 --> 19:54.390
Can you do something, Aoshima?
Then what are we going to do?!

19:54.390 --> 19:55.090
ME?
Then what are we going to do?!

19:55.090 --> 19:55.520
ME?

19:55.890 --> 19:59.390
Leave it to me to be without
tools now of all times!

19:59.390 --> 20:00.730
Get me some water, Satoko!

20:00.730 --> 20:02.760
I thought you said water was no good.

20:02.760 --> 20:05.330
I'll soak my coat and throw it over the pot.

20:05.330 --> 20:08.470
All we need to do is throw some
water on it and that's that!

20:08.470 --> 20:09.470
Stop it!

20:09.470 --> 20:10.490
Shut up!

20:13.010 --> 20:14.130
Look out!

20:15.710 --> 20:16.840
Satoko!

20:17.410 --> 20:18.880
If this keeps up...

20:19.610 --> 20:21.880
Sleep, oh Spirits of Flame!

20:22.220 --> 20:24.810
Let your power slip into profound silence!

20:29.220 --> 20:31.190
Ah, the fire's out...

20:31.590 --> 20:33.660
Are you all right, Otaki?!

20:33.660 --> 20:35.130
Otaki!

20:35.130 --> 20:36.660
I'm all right.

20:36.660 --> 20:38.650
But, your back...

20:38.900 --> 20:40.330
Oh, right.

20:41.270 --> 20:42.900
Check it out.

20:43.070 --> 20:44.570
Thank goodness...

20:44.570 --> 20:46.040
I like you!

20:46.670 --> 20:48.710
That's what I expect of a
Nekomi Tech student!

20:48.710 --> 20:52.380
That's the kind of nerve and decision-making
a mechanic needs to have!

20:52.380 --> 20:55.010
On the other hand, what about you, huh?

20:55.480 --> 21:00.090
Back in my day, I never let a car sit
in the pit for more than 30 seconds!

21:00.090 --> 21:02.590
Y-You mean you used to do that, too?!

21:02.590 --> 21:05.760
Certainly! I'm the one they used to
call me "'Ole Magic Hands" Sho!

21:05.760 --> 21:06.760
WHAT?!

21:06.760 --> 21:08.360
You're the legendary...

21:08.360 --> 21:11.130
As young as you are and you
STILL know about me?!

21:11.130 --> 21:12.800
Yes, I know all about you!

21:12.800 --> 21:16.800
Why, the 1975 Suzuka 8 Hours
is legendary in our circle!

21:16.800 --> 21:17.860
Damn!

21:17.940 --> 21:18.370
Yes, seriously! It's legendary!

21:18.370 --> 21:20.710
Yes, seriously! It's legendary!
Looks like things are all right now.

21:20.710 --> 21:21.340
Yes, seriously! It's legendary!
Yes.

21:21.340 --> 21:21.860
Yes.

21:27.080 --> 21:28.950
Good work.

21:28.950 --> 21:32.290
I'm sorry you always have to
come along to my lectures.

21:32.290 --> 21:35.620
Why do you apologize? I enjoy it.

21:36.220 --> 21:37.950
As long as I'm with you!

21:38.490 --> 21:40.190
Belldandy...

21:42.560 --> 21:44.260
Morisato!

21:44.500 --> 21:46.900
You've gotta help me!
Senior! What is it now?!

21:46.900 --> 21:49.240
Ah, there you are! Otaki!

21:49.240 --> 21:51.840
Look, Otaki! Now HERE'S a good one!

21:51.840 --> 21:53.140
Just look at this!

21:53.510 --> 21:54.840
I never would have guessed that
YOU'RE a collector, too!

21:54.840 --> 21:55.710
N-No, really, it's all right!
I never would have guessed that
YOU'RE a collector, too!

21:55.710 --> 21:57.340
N-No, really, it's all right!
I'm liking you more and more!

21:57.340 --> 22:00.880
Don't hold back! After all,
I'm going to be your father!

22:00.880 --> 22:01.940
Huh?!

22:02.450 --> 22:04.280
I'm so sorry, Otaki!

22:04.280 --> 22:05.150
Satoko?!

22:05.150 --> 22:06.890
I apologize for my father's pushiness!

22:06.890 --> 22:09.260
Here now, Satoko, you ask him, too.

22:09.260 --> 22:11.590
After all, he's going to be
your husband someday!

22:11.590 --> 22:12.890
Dad!

22:13.060 --> 22:14.730
C'mon, Otaki. Try this on.

22:14.730 --> 22:17.030
Whoa! Please hold on a minute,
President Yamano!

22:17.160 --> 22:20.600
I'm no president to you! Call me Dad!

22:20.600 --> 22:24.130
HELP!

22:25.270 --> 22:33.700
Woh, it starts to shine

22:43.190 --> 22:50.490
The gentle wind I felt on my cheek

22:51.830 --> 22:59.260
Was the start of the miracles you brought

22:59.940 --> 23:07.400
As though my everyday life until
then had never existed

23:07.780 --> 23:13.020
My new happy life, completely repainted

23:13.020 --> 23:16.420
In the colors of spring

23:17.090 --> 23:21.360
Even waking up early, even traffic jams

23:21.360 --> 23:25.770
Even heavy things to carry,
even sleepless nights

23:25.770 --> 23:30.100
Somehow I feel thankful for everything

23:30.100 --> 23:34.810
Let's create more and more of our miracles

23:34.810 --> 23:42.650
Woh, whatever kind of morning

23:43.420 --> 23:51.150
Woh, it starts to shine

23:51.860 --> 23:54.660
Every day is a miracle

23:55.900 --> 23:58.570
There is someone who wants to
express her feelings for you.

23:58.570 --> 24:03.060
But, those feelings draw her towards
darkness before she realizes it.

24:03.170 --> 24:04.570
Next time, "Ah! Is That Jealousy?!"

24:04.570 --> 24:05.970
Ah! Is That Jealousy?!
Next time, "Ah! Is That Jealousy?!"

24:05.970 --> 24:08.980
Ah! Is That Jealousy?!
I-Is this one of those so-called
"love letters"?!

24:08.980 --> 24:09.500
Ah! Is That Jealousy?!
